#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197955 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f44e99a-00a9-5df9-bf70-c3e9b14260fa" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/id #uuid "0f1a2a41-b97f-5ac7-a51d-a90cb3ba366a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12368" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{x} \\int_{0}^{3-x-y} x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}∫_{0}^{3 - x - y}xdzdydx &= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}[∫_{0}^{3 - x - y}xdz]dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}x \\cdot [z]_{z = 0}^{z = 3 - x - y}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}x(3 - x - y)dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydydx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydydx &= ∫_{0}^{2}[∫_{0}^{x}3x - x^{2} - xydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}[(3x - x^{2})y - \\frac{1}{2}xy^{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}(3x - x^{2})(x - 0) - \\frac{1}{2}x(x^{2} - 0)dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - x^{3} - \\frac{1}{2}x^{3}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - \\frac{3}{2}x^{3}dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}3x^{2} - \\frac{3}{2}x^{3}dx &= [x^{3} - \\frac{3}{8}x^{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = 2} \\\\\n&= 8 - 6 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197963 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab856632-0413-5d1d-8b5b-90e75f5bc1b6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "2ad7b82c-8624-5a59-8a2c-c5c1852e6cf6" :question/math-academy-id "e-12389" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2} \\int_{-1}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} x^2y+xz^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y$." :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}y + xz^{2}dzdxdy &= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}[∫_{0}^{1}x^{2}y + xz^{2}dz]dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}[x^{2}yz + \\frac{xz^{3}}{3}]_{z = 0}^{z = 1}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y(1 - 0) + x(\\frac{1}{3} - 0)dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdxdy &= ∫_{1}^{2}[∫_{-1}^{2}x^{2}y + \\frac{1}{3}xdx]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{3}x^{3}y + \\frac{1}{6}x^{2}]_{x =-1}^{x = 2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}y(2^{3} - (-1)^{3}) + \\frac{1}{6}(2^{2} - (-1)^{2}))dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}3y + \\frac{1}{2}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}3y + \\frac{1}{2}dx &= [\\frac{3y^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y}{2}]_{y = 1}^{y = 2} \\\\\n&= (6 + 1) - (\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197964 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4680f2f-fa39-5942-b1fb-6c48a307a439" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals Using the Sum and Product Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "5a596157-d6dd-528d-912c-52889780567d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12390" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Since the domain of integration\n\n$$\nR = [1,2] \\times \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right] \\times [1,4]\n$$\n\nis a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z)$, we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{π/2}∫_{1}^{4}\\frac{\\sin y}{x}dzdydx &= ∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{dx}{x}∫_{0}^{π/2}\\sin ydy∫_{1}^{4}dz\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}dx∫_{0}^{π/2}\\sin ydy∫_{1}^{4}dz &= [\\ln \\mid x \\mid ]_{1}^{2} \\cdot [- \\cos y]_{0}^{π/2} \\cdot (4 - 1) \\\\\n&= (\\ln 2 - \\ln 1) \\cdot (-\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) + \\cos (0)) \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= (\\ln 2 - 0) \\cdot (0 + 1) \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 3\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2} \\int_{1}^{4} \\dfrac{\\sin{y}}{x} \\: \\textrm{d}z \\: \\textrm{d}y \\: \\textrm{d}x = 3\\ln 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab856632-0413-5d1d-8b5b-90e75f5bc1b6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88970e4d-f54f-5484-b730-94f8fadd1366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197630} {:answer/id #uuid "c243b024-2af1-58aa-89f2-12d11c7f9ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197631} {:answer/id #uuid "e06d748a-7e07-581a-9661-ba0029ce01eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197632} {:answer/id #uuid "5f10e338-3bb8-5158-bad2-5c8f254ba031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197633} {:answer/id #uuid "75ea090a-55ba-5410-bc1b-8fd6ad53db75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f10e338-3bb8-5158-bad2-5c8f254ba031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197633} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2d2ccaf-6ed3-5944-89e9-da594761ca27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197629}] :question/id #uuid "5259e1b9-028d-504a-ac38-55eae4d0c29a" :question/math-academy-id "q-39476" :question/problem "What is $∫_{0}^{1}∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{2}xy + yz + xzdxdydz$?"}]}
